From: Armada <armada@armada.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: smp2p: reset input state only on restart

With SSR acknowledgements negotiated, qcom_smp2p_check_ssr() clears
last_value on every interrupt, even when the restart flag has not changed.
The subsequent change detection therefore loses falling edges and can
deliver duplicate rising-edge interrupts for unchanged high inputs.

On the Duo, WLAN wake succeeds but the release acknowledgment times out:
firmware clears bit 0, while smp2p_notify_in reports status 0.
Return before clearing the saved input values unless a restart is detected.
Keep the existing reset and acknowledgment behavior for actual restarts.

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
@@ -194,6 +194,9 @@ static bool qcom_smp2p_check_ssr(struct qcom_smp2p *smp2p)
 
 	restart_done = in->flags & BIT(SMP2P_FLAGS_RESTART_DONE_BIT);
 	restart = restart_done != smp2p->ssr_ack;
+	if (!restart)
+		return false;
+
 	list_for_each_entry(entry, &smp2p->inbound, node) {
 		if (!entry->value)
 			continue;
